In addition to the personalized greeting, the server should also generate a random number between 1 and 100, and display it on the HTML page.

Furthermore, the server should implement form validation to check if the user enters a valid name. The name should be at least 3 characters long and should not contain any special characters or numbers. If the user enters an invalid name, the server should display an appropriate error message in the generated HTML page.

The server should handle cases where the user does not enter a name or submits an empty input by displaying a generic error message in the generated HTML page.

Note: The server should use pure NodeJS without any external libraries or frameworks. The server should also aim for efficient time complexity and avoid unnecessary computations.

