Create a NodeJS server that listens on port 8080 and serves a simple HTML page. However, the HTML page should be dynamically generated based on user input.

When a GET request is made to the server, it should prompt the user to enter their name. The server should then take the user's name and generate an HTML page that includes a personalized greeting.

For example, if the user enters "John" as their name, the server should generate an HTML page that displays "Hello, John!" as the greeting.

The server should also implement error handling for cases where the user does not enter a name or submits an empty input. In these cases, the server should display an error message in the generated HTML page.

Note: The server should use pure NodeJS without any external libraries or frameworks.

### Response:
Here's an example of how you can create a NodeJS server that dynamically generates an HTML page based on user input:

```javascript
const http = require('http');
const url = require('url');
const querystring = require('querystring');

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
  const { pathname, query } = url.parse(req.url);
  const { name } = querystring.parse(query);

  if (req.method === 'GET' && pathname === '/') {
    res.statusCode = 200;
    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/html');

    let body = '<html><body>';
    body += '<h1>Enter your name:</h1>';
    body += '<form method="POST" action="/greet">';
    body += '<input type="text" name="name" />';
    body += '<input type="submit" value="Submit" />';
    body += '</form>';
    body += '</body></html>';

    res.end(body);
  } else if (req.method === 'POST' && pathname === '/greet') {
    if (!name || name.trim() === '') {
      res.statusCode = 400;
      res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/html');
      res.end('<html><body><h1>Error: Please enter a name</h1></body></html>');
    } else {
      res.statusCode = 200;
      res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/html');
      res.end(`<html><body><h1>Hello, ${name}!</h1></body></html>`);
    }
  } else {
    res.statusCode = 404;
    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/html');
    res.end('<html><body><h1>Error: Page not found</h1></body></html>');
  }
});

server.listen(8080, () => {
  console.log('Server is running on port 8080');
});
```

This code creates a NodeJS server that listens on port 8080. When a GET request is made to the server, it prompts the user to enter their name. When a POST request is made to the "/greet" endpoint, it generates an HTML page with a personalized greeting.

The server implements error handling by checking if the user did not enter a name or submitted an empty input. In these cases, it displays an error message in the generated HTML page.

To run this code, save it to a file (e.g., `server.js`) and run `node server.js` in the terminal. Then, you can access the server by opening a web browser and navigating to `http://localhost:8080`.

